# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# agent scratch space — .claude/worktrees holds nested git checkouts,
# which git will not track correctly and which must never ship.
.claude/

# generated quote/price artifacts, including real client documents
scripts/out/

# one-off read-only probes: written to answer a single question about the live
# database, kept only so the next person can see what was asked. They are not
# maintained, nothing imports them, and no test pins them -- so committing one
# publishes an unmaintained query against production as if it were a tool.
# dfb4b0a committed scripts/diag-unpriced-shipments.mjs by accident this way.
#
# Deliberately NOT a `diag-*` rule: 15 diag- scripts are tracked and 9 are not,
# so that pattern would claim to ignore files git is already tracking and tell
# a reader the opposite of the truth. Every probe-* is untracked and no tracked
# file begins with probe-, so this one matches exactly what it says it does.
# `git add -f` is the escape hatch if a probe ever earns its place.
scripts/probe-*

# The scratch diag- scripts, named in full because the glob above cannot reach
# them: 15 OTHER diag- scripts are tracked, so `scripts/diag-*` would claim to
# ignore files git is already tracking.
#
# Listed one per line rather than as `scripts/diag-*` plus a `!` exception for
# each of the 15 tracked ones. That would have been fewer characters but it
# would restate, in this file, a fact git already holds -- which of these are
# tracked -- and the copy would go stale silently the next time one is added or
# untracked. Each line below instead names a file that is scratch today; if one
# is deleted the line is dead but harmless, and it cannot disagree with git.
#
# The cost of doing it this way: a FUTURE diag- script is not covered, so the
# dfb4b0a accident can still happen to one that does not exist yet. Accepted,
# because the alternative hides the opposite mistake -- a new diagnostic that
# was meant to be tracked, silently ignored, with nothing in `git status` to
# show it. `git add -f` is the escape hatch either way.
scripts/diag-unpriced-shipments.mjs
scripts/diag-carrier-card-gap.mjs
scripts/diag-carrier-zone-mismatch.mjs
scripts/diag-legacy-clientkey.mjs
scripts/diag-order-items.mjs
scripts/diag-warehouse-rates.mjs
scripts/diag-zone-chart-coverage.mjs
scripts/diag-zone-chart-diff.mjs
scripts/diag-zone-chart-provenance.mjs

# Supabase CLI scratch — version cache, not source
supabase/.temp/
